        S("Walk backward to compute return", "Start with G = 0 at termination. Each backward step reuses the return already computed for the next state.", active=1, equation="G ← r + γG"),
        S("Select the visits", "First-visit MC uses the earliest occurrence of a state in the episode. Every-visit MC uses all occurrences; a backward seen-set would pick the wrong first visit.", active=2, equation="First visit means earliest in forward time."),
